    <h3 id="status-filter-ticket-title">Add a status filter to the existing orders list</h3>
    <dl class="tracking-ticket-metadata"><div><dt>Created by</dt><dd>Product</dd></div><div><dt>Priority</dt><dd class="tracking-ticket-priority">Medium</dd></div></dl>
  </header>
  <div class="tracking-ticket-body">
    <section>
      <h4>Existing behavior</h4>
      <p>Orders have <code>pending</code>, <code>completed</code>, or <code>cancelled</code> status. The list uses server-side pagination.</p>
    </section>
    <section>
      <h4>Required behavior</h4>
      <p>Offer those statuses and “All,” which means no status filter and is the default. Changing the selection resets the list to page 1 and preserves the current sort order.</p>
    </section>
    <section>
      <h4>Constraints</h4>
      <p>Use the existing list components and query conventions. Apply filtering before pagination, including the pagination totals. Preserve existing access checks.</p>
    </section>
    <section>
      <h4>Acceptance criteria</h4>
      <ul class="tracking-ticket-checklist">
        <li>“All” preserves the current results.</li>
        <li>Each status returns only matching orders, including matches beyond the original first page, with correct totals.</li>
        <li>Switching filters resets the page without changing the sort.</li>
        <li>Users still see only orders they are allowed to access.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>
    <section>
      <h4>Out of scope</h4>
      <p>New statuses, schema changes, a page redesign, or a new caching layer. Report unrelated bugs separately.</p>
    </section>
  </div>
